// Asserted to stay OPEN by RulesTest#unsoundWfProblemStaysOpen: conformsMapElem hands out
// conformance at every Prim key (at(TRUE) too), so conformsMapRight must owe it at a fresh Prim key.
// With an int skolem, conformance at the int keys alone proved the mapping atom. The problem
// needs HeuristicInstantiation to skip ill-sorted instances: instantiating i with the Prim
// skolem used to abort the proof with an illegal instantiation.

\functions {
    Struct st;
}

\problem {
    (\forall int i; conforms(emptyOf<[int[3]]>, selectSt<[Struct]>(st, at(i))))
        -> conforms(emptyOf<[mapping<[int, int[3]]>]>, st)
}
